From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: edwardzhu02 <explodingtnt@foxmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 22:27:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] stmp3770: run the GPMI from HF (PLL/2) like ExistOS

With the pin mux in place the NAND bus came alive on hardware: page 0 and
page 1984 read back the same bytes as the 128 MB backup, but every read
started one byte late (page 0 gave 54 4d 50 2d instead of 53 54 4d 50).

The descriptors and timing constants are identical to ExistOS, so the
remaining difference is the GPMI clock source: we had it on the 24 MHz
crystal, ExistOS runs it at HF (PLL 480 MHz / 2) with GPMIFreq 240 MHz.
The BootROM leaves the PLL powered (PLLCTRL0.POWER set), so switch back
to that setting.
---
 arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_gpmi.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_gpmi.c b/arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_gpmi.c
index 6313f68c..122d9c0a 100644
--- a/arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_gpmi.c
+++ b/arch/arm/src/stmp3770/stmp3770_gpmi.c
@@ -163,12 +163,13 @@ static void GPMI_ClockConfigure()
     HW_CLKCTRL_GPMI_WR(BF_CLKCTRL_GPMI_DIV(2));
     INFO("GPMI CLK DIV:%d\n", BF_RD(CLKCTRL_GPMI, DIV));
 
-    /* 真机上没有跑 stmp3770_clockconfig()（会卡死芯片），PLL 状态未知。
-     * GPMI 直接旁路到 24 MHz 晶振，时序常数按 24 MHz 算，慢但一定能跑。 */
+    /* 与 ExistOS 一致：走 HF（PLL 480 MHz / 2）。BootROM 已经把 PLL 上电
+     * （PLLCTRL0.POWER=1）。真机上按 24 MHz 晶振算时序时，读回来的数据整体
+     * 错开一个字节（采样点对不上），所以必须用 PLL 这个时钟域。 */
 
-    BF_SET(CLKCTRL_CLKSEQ, BYPASS_GPMI);
+    BF_CLR(CLKCTRL_CLKSEQ, BYPASS_GPMI);
 
-    GPMIFreq = 24000000ULL;
+    GPMIFreq = 480000000ULL / 2ULL;
 
 
 }
